# No Co-authored-by / No Cursor commit UI

## Hard ban

- **NEVER** add `Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by`, or any other trailer that attributes the commit to Cursor, an agent, or a tool.
- **NEVER** use Cursor's commit UI, commit harness, Source Control commit button, or any IDE-mediated commit flow that may inject trailers.
- **ONLY** create commits by running plain `git commit` in the **Shell** tool with a HEREDOC message.

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — shell only
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Commit title here

- Optional bullet
EOF
)"

# ❌ BAD — anything that lets Cursor wrap/inject the commit
# (Source Control panel, "Commit" UI actions, agent commit helpers)
```

## After every commit

Run `git log -1 --format='%B'` and confirm the body has **no** `Co-authored-by` (or similar). If one was injected somehow, remove it immediately with a new commit or an amend **only** when amend rules already allow it; prefer stripping before the commit lands if possible.

